      "proof_review": {
        "reviewed": true,
        "context_checked": true,
        "method": "Published author proof/core and local context fidelity screening",
        "note": "Read the complete Theorem4.6 proof and the explicit positive/negative annihilation formulas (3.1)–(3.2). The double Fock construction is on the complexification of a separable real Hilbert space, alpha,q in (-1,1), and selected arguments are real simple tensors. The underlying Coxeter positivity and parabolic decomposition are prior established results. The adjoint identification Proposition3.6 is the elementary construction obtained from that decomposition; its explicit resulting operator formula is present and used by the proof. The omitted norm estimates in Theorem3.9 are not needed for this algebraic vacuum-moment identity and are not claimed. All partition statistics, both inductive cases and the exhaustive final pairing sum are retained."
      },
